==Battleground==
*1 [[Cyberhorn]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Calamary|Calamaries]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*8 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Nimoy Bore]] spawns after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Another stage full of [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, just like [[2nd Round: Dawn (Expert)]]. You will need [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], except this time you will need every single [[Aqua Crystal]] and [[Plasma Crystal]] [[Treasure]] from each [[Into the Future]] chapter. In other words, you need all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] for this stage to become manageable for the average player. Cyberhorn spawns almost immediately, and he is at 600%, so [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] and/or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] can really help keep him from pushing too much. There are also two Calamaries, which can be really annoying if you didn't bring a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]] like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or a unit that can outrange Calamary. The Helmut Krabbes and Shibaliens do not matter, but the Ursamajors are quite strong so [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] can be helpful against them. There is also a Nimoy Bore that spawns after ~93 seconds, so you must be prepared if you are taking a long time to beat the stage, but you can most likely just use the same units you used against Cyberhorn to defeat him.

